---@class gcp.unstable.cloudsupport_v2beta.PatchCasesRequest
---@field displayName? string The short summary of the issue reported in this case.
---@field severity? gcp.unstable.cloudsupport_v2beta.CaseSeverityEnum|string REMOVED. The severity of this case. Use priority instead.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time this case was last updated.
---@field subscriberEmailAddresses? gcp.unstable.cloudsupport_v2beta.StringList The email addresses to receive updates on this case.
---@field description? string A broad description of the issue.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time this case was created.
---@field contactEmail? string A user-supplied email address to send case update notifications for. This field must be set when the request is authenticated using a Workforce Identity Federation (BYOID) flow and must not be set otherwise. When unset, the contact email is inferred from the authenticated user's credentials. If you use a service account to create the case and its inferred email address cannot receive emails, you should add appropriate contact emails in the `subscriber_email_addresses` field.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.cloudsupport_v2beta.CaseStateEnum|string Output only. The current status of the support case.
---@field creator? gcp.unstable.cloudsupport_v2beta.Actor The user who created the case. This field is ignored on input. Note: The name and email will be obfuscated if the case was created by Google Support.
---@field timeZone? string The timezone of the user who created the support case. It should be in a format IANA recognizes: https://www.iana.org/time-zones. There is no additional validation done by the API.
---@field testCase? boolean Whether this case was created for internal API testing and should not be acted on by the support team.
---@field escalated? boolean Whether the case is currently escalated.
---@field priority? gcp.unstable.cloudsupport_v2beta.CasePriorityEnum|string The priority of this case.
---@field classification? gcp.unstable.cloudsupport_v2beta.CaseClassification The issue classification applicable to this case.
---@field languageCode? string The language the user has requested to receive support in. This should be a BCP 47 language code (e.g., `"en"`, `"zh-CN"`, `"zh-TW"`, `"ja"`, `"ko"`). If no language or an unsupported language is specified, this field defaults to English (en). Language selection during case creation may affect your available support options. For a list of supported languages and their support working hours, see: https://cloud.google.com/support/docs/language-working-hours
---@field name string Identifier. The resource name for the case.
---@field updateMask? string A list of attributes of the case that should be updated. Supported values are `priority`, `display_name`, and `subscriber_email_addresses`. If no fields are specified, all supported fields are updated. Be careful - if you do not provide a field mask, then you might accidentally clear some fields. For example, if you leave the field mask empty and do not provide a value for `subscriber_email_addresses`, then `subscriber_email_addresses` is updated to empty.

